# {{.ProjectName}}

An event-driven application built with Go, implementing CQRS and Event Sourcing patterns.

## Architecture

This application implements:
- **CQRS (Command Query Responsibility Segregation)**
- **Event Sourcing** with complete audit trail
- **Domain-Driven Design (DDD)** patterns
- **Event Store** with {{.DatabaseType}} backend
- **Message Queue** using {{.MessageQueue}}
- **Read Model Projections** for optimized queries
- **Saga Pattern** for complex workflows

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Go {{.GoVersion}}+
- {{title .DatabaseType}} database
- {{title .MessageQueue}} message queue

### Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone {{.ModulePath}}.git
cd {{.ProjectName}}

# Install dependencies
go mod tidy

# Run the application
go run main.go
```

### Configuration

Copy and modify the configuration file:

```bash
cp configs/config.yaml.example configs/config.yaml
# Edit configs/config.yaml with your settings
```

## API Endpoints

- `GET /health` - Health check
- `POST /api/v1/users` - Create user (Command)
- `GET /api/v1/users` - Get users (Query)
- `POST /api/v1/orders` - Create order (Command)
- `GET /api/v1/orders` - Get orders (Query)

## Event Store

The application uses {{.DatabaseType}} as the event store backend. Events are persisted with metadata including:
- Event ID
- Event Type
- Event Data
- Event Version
- Timestamp
- Correlation ID

## Message Queue

Events are published to {{.MessageQueue}} for:
- Real-time notifications
- Cross-service communication
- Event replay capabilities

## Development

### Running Tests

```bash
# Run all tests
go test ./...

# Run tests with coverage
go test -cover ./...
```

### Building for Production

```bash
# Build binary
go build -o bin/{{.ProjectName}} .

# Build Docker image
docker build -t {{.ProjectName}} .
```

## Project Structure

```
.
├── main.go                          # Application entry point
├── internal/
│   ├── domain/                      # Domain layer (aggregates, events, commands)
│   ├── application/                 # Application services
│   ├── infrastructure/              # Infrastructure layer
│   ├── api/                         # HTTP handlers and routes
│   ├── cqrs/                        # CQRS command/query buses
│   ├── eventstore/                  # Event store implementations
│   ├── eventbus/                    # Event publishing
│   ├── projections/                 # Read model projections
│   └── sagas/                       # Saga implementations
├── migrations/                      # Database migrations
├── configs/                         # Configuration files
└── test/                           # Test fixtures and helpers
```

